This test exercises the "GPU_CollideStream_Iolets_Ladd_VelBCs" kernels.
This is related to velocity boundary conditions in HemeLB and is similar to repro_Ladd_Vel_BCs.

There is a 'functorized version' of the kernel as well as just a regular __global__ function. 
The functor version fails to reproduce the results of the kernel version unless a 

__syncthreads(); ( or in some cases printf()s ) are introduced at line 107 of  GPU_Collide_Stream_Iolets.hpp

This test reuses the input date from precursor_data_7.h, but because it uses a different kernel
doesn't have reference output data. Instead it compares the results of the two kernels called to each other.


Files:

api.h :   Kernel launchig + macros (mini portable API implemented in HIP)

GPU_Collide_Stream_wall_sBB_Iolets.hpp:

	This contains the kernels both the functor form and the '__global__' function form
	The file also contains a device function the kernels call.
	Finally the '__global__ function' version relies on some constant memory so this file
	contains a setup() function to fill the constant memory symbols from the 'nash_data_1.h' file

precursor_data_7.h: the input data to the kernels and expected output data -- dumped from process 7 of the original test

main.cu: the test code (applies both the Functor, and reglar kernel version of the code and compares
against referens)


NB: There is overall only 1 compilation unit. main.cu includes GPU_Collide_Stream_Iolets.hpp, which
in turn incldes the api.h and nash_data_1.h file.

To run, just run:  

make

Failing test output looks like:

[bjoo@login2.crusher repro3]$ make

